    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d366">

                <pb facs="1071" n="1065" xml:id="pg1065"/>

                <head>No. 19.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. C. J.
                            McCarthy to Mr. C. B.
                        Wilson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1893-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1,
                                1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">C. B. Wilson</hi>:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: As per your request of to-day I
                    inclose you a diagram of the position of the <hi rendition="#italic">Boston</hi>
                    troops as of Monday evening, January 16, 1893. They remained in the third
                    position for several days.</p>
                <figure>
                    <graphic url="figure_1071"/>
                </figure>
                <p>In connection with the arrival of the committee of safety, I would say that they
                    arrived at the Government building at 2:30 p.m. on <pb facs="1072" n="1066"
                        xml:id="pg1066"/> Tuesday, January 17, loitered about the corridor a few
                    minutes, asked Mr. Hossinger for possession of the building, and then Mr. Cooper
                    proceeded to read the proclamation. He finished same at 2:10 p.m., at which time
                    I received your telephone message and came to the station house.</p>
                <p>Yours, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. J. McCarthy.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
